# Project Design Phase

## Project Title: ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

### 1. Introduction

The project design phase explains the overall structure, architecture, modules, and workflow of the ComicCraft application.

ComicCraft is an AI-powered comic story creator that uses Google Gemini models to transform user ideas into creative comic stories. It helps users generate storylines, characters, dialogues, and comic panel descriptions through a simple and interactive interface.

The main objective of this phase is to design a system that is easy to use, efficient, and capable of supporting AI-based comic story creation.

**GitHub Repository:** ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models.


### 2. System Architecture Design

ComicCraft is designed using a modular architecture with three major layers:

1. **Frontend Layer:** Provides the interface for entering story prompts, selecting genres, and viewing comic panels.
2. **Backend Layer:** Processes user inputs, communicates with the Gemini API, and manages generated content.
3. **AI Layer:** Generates storylines, character descriptions, dialogues, and comic scene descriptions.

The design follows a structured AI comic-generation workflow, where story and panel information can be organized into structured data before visual generation. ([github.com][1])

